      "provenance": {
        "notes": "An integer exponent above 31 leaves the exact integer-power route and is carried as f32, but f32 cannot separate consecutive integers past 2^24: 16777217 rounds to an even value. A negative base then takes the sign of the wrong parity even though the answer, plus or minus one, is exact at every exponent. Zero tolerance -- the middle entry is the only even one."
